# Quantia Web — Project Rules (always active)

## Product
Quantia is a web platform to manage research projects of the INNOVATEK'S / GITEMOS research seedbed.
This repository contains ONLY the frontend client (Next.js). Users have three roles:
Investigador (Researcher), Coordinador (Coordinator) and Administrador (Administrator).
Tone: institutional, sober, clear, trustworthy. Color communicates state; it is never decoration.
Code, components and tokens in English; all user-facing UI copy in Spanish.

## Locked stack — NEVER change without written approval
- Runtime: Node.js 22 LTS, TypeScript strict mode.
- Framework: Next.js (App Router) + React. Version pinned in package.json.
- Styling: Styled Components with a typed `theme` (light + dark) and an SSR registry
  (`StyleSheetManager` + `useServerInsertedHTML`) so there is no FOUC and no hydration mismatch.
  Components using styled-components are Client Components ("use client").
- Primitives: Radix UI (accessible base for dialogs, menus, selects, tooltips, tabs, etc.).
- Motion: Framer Motion. Charts: Recharts.
- Real time: Socket.io client against the API (namespaces `/projects`, `/notifications` and `/general`).
- Data contracts: `@quantia/contracts` (TS types + Zod schemas), shared with the API.
- Design source of truth: Figma library + `DESIGN.md` (same token/component names in both).
- Deploy: Vercel (frontend only). API, worker and Redis live on Railway.

## Shadcn policy (decided)
- Shadcn is a PATTERN REFERENCE only. Never run the Shadcn CLI, never copy its Tailwind classes,
  never add Tailwind, `clsx`/`tailwind-merge`/`cva` or any Shadcn-generated file.
- Build every component as: Radix primitive + Styled Components + theme tokens, following Shadcn's
  composition/anatomy ideas (compound components, `asChild`, controlled/uncontrolled props).
- A component exists only if it is registered in `DESIGN.md` (and in the Figma library).

## Architecture invariants (non-negotiable)
1. The Quantia API (`/api/v1`) is the ONLY backend the browser talks to (plus its Socket.io gateway).
   Never access Supabase, Notion or Redis from the browser, and never import their SDKs.
2. All request/response types and Zod schemas come from `@quantia/contracts`. Never hand-write or
   duplicate a contract. If a contract is missing, stop and flag it instead of inventing types.
3. Navigation and landing view are GENERATED from the roles returned by `GET /users/me` (never by
   decoding the JWT) (Investigador: "Mis tareas";
   Coordinador: group dashboard; Administrador: institutional view). Sections without permission
   are not rendered.
4. Hiding UI does NOT replace authorization. The API is the authority; always handle 401/403 from it.
   403 messages never reveal the existence of out-of-scope resources.
5. One feature folder per domain (`features/projects`, `tasks`, `progress`, `budget`, `reports`,
   `audit`, `sync`). No business logic inside UI components; use typed hooks/services per feature.
6. One single API client (silent refresh, one retry, normalized errors). No ad-hoc `fetch` in components.
7. Real-time events never reorder or move content under the cursor (highlight 1–2 s instead).
   Socket.io connects to the long-running API, never to Next.js route handlers or serverless functions.

## Design System rules
- Component names, props and tokens mirror Figma: `intent="primary"`, `size="md"`, `isLoading`,
  `theme.colors.brand.primary`, `theme.space[4]`, `theme.typography.bodyMedium`.
- Only theme tokens for color, spacing, radii, elevation, typography and motion. Dark mode is solved
  in tokens, never per component.
- Every component implements default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading and error
  (when applicable). Reuse registered components in `src/components/{base,system,composite,page}`
  before creating anything.
- Always implement technical → visual states: skeleton, empty, error, 401 (session modal),
  403, 429 (auto retry), sync pending/failed, long job, WebSocket disconnected.

## Security defaults
- Access JWT in memory only (never localStorage/sessionStorage). Refresh token lives in an httpOnly cookie set
  by the Next session route handlers (`src/app/api/session/*`); it is never readable by JS.
- Validate socket payloads always, and API responses in development, with Zod from contracts. Never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with API/user data.
- Files only via signed short-lived URLs returned by the API.
- Destructive actions require `ConfirmDialog`. Never log tokens, PII or budget data.
- Only non-secret values in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` (API origin, app environment).

## Coding conventions
- One component per file, props interface `[ComponentName]Props`, TypeScript strict.
- Every list is paginated (`page`, `pageSize`); filters and sort live in the URL.
- Formats: COP currency, DD/MM/AAAA dates, percentages with max 1 decimal.
- Animations 150/200/250 ms, `transform`/`opacity` only, honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Charts always show visible values and offer a table alternative.
- Accessibility WCAG 2.1 AA: contrast >= 4.5:1 (3:1 large text/borders), 16 px base text,
  44x44 px touch targets, full keyboard navigation, persistent labels.
- Branches `feature/*` -> PR -> `main`. No direct commits to `main`. Conventional Commits.

## Critical DON'Ts
- Do NOT hardcode hex colors or loose px values (spacing, radii, font sizes, shadows). Use theme tokens.
- Do NOT create or use components that are not registered in `DESIGN.md`.
- Do NOT add a new dependency, library or provider without asking first.
- Do NOT use `any` or `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` to silence the compiler.
- Do NOT put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables or anywhere in the client bundle.
- Do NOT remove or override `:focus-visible` styles (`outline: none` without an equivalent ring is forbidden).
- Do NOT call Supabase, Notion or Redis from the browser.
- Do NOT rely on hidden UI for authorization.
- Do NOT disable lint rules, a11y checks or tests, and do NOT skip tests to make CI pass.

## Verification before saying a task is done
1. `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` pass with zero errors.
2. axe reports zero violations on every screen touched (all states and both themes).
3. A screenshot of the implemented screen is compared against its Figma frame
   (390, 768 and 1280 px) and any deviation is fixed or flagged for design approval.
4. No hardcoded hex/px, no `any`, types come from `@quantia/contracts`.
5. Role check: each role sees only its navigation and views; 401/403 handled.

## Documentation map — read the right file (do not invent paths)

| File | Role | When to read |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `.cursorrules` | Locked stack, invariants, DON'Ts | Always (this file) |
| `AGENTS.md` | Agent workflow, repo map, commands, DoD | Always before acting |
| `DESIGN.md` | Tokens, registered components, patterns | Before ANY UI work |
| `.cursor/docs/SCREENS.md` | Screen inventory, routes, roles, blueprints | Any screen / route task |
| `.cursor/docs/frontend-conventions.md` | Folders, Figma→code, Git/PR, DoD, env | Structure, PR, setup |
| `.cursor/docs/api-connection.md` | Frontend↔API connection (F3: HTTP, session, sockets, sync, reports, errors) | Integration, onboarding, realtime/sync/reports work |
| `.cursor/rules/ui-design-system.mdc` | Thin UI rule → points to `DESIGN.md` | `src/components/**`, `src/theme/**`, `*.styles.ts` |
| `.cursor/rules/accessibility-ux.mdc` | A11y, copy, formats, focus, charts | `src/app/**`, `src/components/**` |
| `.cursor/rules/api-integration.mdc` | Contracts, client, session, sockets, roles | `src/lib/**`, `src/features/**`, `src/app/**` |

Load only the modular rule(s) that match the area you touch. Paths above are canonical —
never use `docs/SCREENS.md`, `docs/frontend-conventions.md`, or bare `ui-design-system.md`.